From: Garnet local integration
Subject: [PATCH 31/31] radv/darwin: enable async compute ring, dual-ring sync, and gang submit

Sync RDNA4N_HW_IP_COMPUTE (1u), RDNA4N_CAP_ASYNC_COMPUTE (1u << 6), and
RDNA4N_SEQ_RING_COMPUTE (1ull << 62) into include/darwin/rdna4_native_abi.h
and ac_darwin_kext.c.

When QueryInfo.flags advertises RDNA4N_CAP_ASYNC_COMPUTE:
  - AMDGPU_INFO_HW_IP_INFO(AMDGPU_HW_IP_COMPUTE) reports available_rings = 1
    (keeping available_rings = 0 on older kernels, garnet-async-compute=0, and
    the mock transport), exposing a dedicated Vulkan compute queue family and
    automatically unlocking VK_SHADER_STAGE_TASK_BIT_EXT (Task + Mesh) in 0029.
  - ac_darwin_sync.c tracks per-ring retirement (known_retired[2] indexed by
    seqno bit 62), polls both rings in wait_generic() and sync_query(), and
    waits on cross-ring dependencies in acd_sync_cs_wait_ready() while keeping
    same-ring dependencies lock-free.
  - acd_kext_submit() partitions mixed COMPUTE + GFX gang submissions (used by
    RADV Task+Mesh) so the ACE follower IBs launch on KCQ immediately before
    the GFX leader IBs launch on the GFX ring for true concurrent execution.
  - acd_cmd_gem_wait_idle() drains both the GFX ring and the compute ring.

Base: f5cb8ee032adabef599ae892ec4e42d796b84da9 + patches 0001..0030.

